-- Tier 1 and tier 2 tests.
--
-- Tier 1 is the test table on the left of Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov
-- & Gelbard (2025), the SimpLEX screen capture, transcribed row for row and
-- run against the text it was written for: the draft.
--
-- Tier 2 runs the SAME four scenarios against the two texts that came after
-- the draft -- the Regulations as made (16 July 2025) and as amended (5786) --
-- and asserts what each of them actually answers. Every assertion here is
-- satisfied; the point is that the answers move. The companion file
-- hvac-tests-simplex-red.l4 runs the draft's EXPECTATIONS against the
-- Regulations as made and is meant to fail, and check.sh counts its failures.
@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-fees`

§ `Tier 1 -- the SimpLEX test table, in its own words`

-- SimpLEX's table has three columns: scenario, expected outcome, citation. Its
-- outcomes are the three phrases below, not TRUE and FALSE, so the rows are
-- asserted here in exactly those words. (The screenshot's second table, "test
-- scenarios for fee updates and the index", shows only its heading and its
-- citations -- Law s.59, regs 2(a)-(c) -- so its rows cannot be transcribed.)
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `registration approved`     -- הרשמה מאושרת
    `appeal under review`       -- הערעור נבדק
    `registration refused`      -- הרשמה נדחית

GIVEN vintage IS A Vintage
      service IS A Service
      paid    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Outcome
DECIDE `the SimpLEX outcome under` @nlg what SimpLEX's table would show for %service% under %vintage% when %paid% shekels have been paid
                                  @nlg:he מה שטבלת SimpLEX הייתה מציגה בעד %service% לפי %vintage% כאשר שולמו %paid% שקלים
    IS IF NOT `the service may be provided` vintage service paid
       THEN `registration refused`
       ELSE CONSIDER service
            WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN `appeal under review`
            WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN `appeal under review`
            OTHERWISE `registration approved`

-- #  scenario                                            expected outcome           citation
-- 5  registration for a theoretical examination          registration approved      reg. 2(a)
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the SimpLEX draft` `theoretical examination` 273 EQUALS `registration approved`
-- 6  registration for a practical examination            registration approved      reg. 2(b)
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the SimpLEX draft` `practical examination` 194 EQUALS `registration approved`
-- 7  appeal with payment (40 NIS)                        appeal under review        reg. 2(c)
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the SimpLEX draft` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 40 EQUALS `appeal under review`
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the SimpLEX draft` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40 EQUALS `appeal under review`
-- 8  registration for an examination without payment    registration refused       reg. 4
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the SimpLEX draft` `theoretical examination` 0 EQUALS `registration refused`
#ASSERT `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the SimpLEX draft` `practical examination` 0 EQUALS `registration refused`

-- The same four rows, as the Regulations as made would have shown them:
#EVAL `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the Regulations as made` `theoretical examination` 273
#EVAL `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the Regulations as made` `theoretical examination` 0
#EVAL `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 40
#EVAL `the SimpLEX outcome under` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40

§ `Tier 1 -- the SimpLEX test table, against the draft it was written for`

-- Fig. 4, "test scenarios for professional examinations", relevant provisions
-- "Law -- s.9 | Regulations -- 2(a)-(h)":
--   #5  registration for a theoretical examination  -> registration approved   (reg. 2(a))
--   #6  registration for a practical examination    -> registration approved   (reg. 2(b))
--   #7  appeal with payment (40 NIS)                -> appeal under review      (reg. 2(c))
--   #8  registration for an examination, no payment -> registration refused    (reg. 4)
-- and the worked example beneath the table: "the candidate registered for a
-- theoretical examination but did not pay the fee ... outcome: registration
-- refused -- a duty to pay the fee".

#ASSERT `the fee under` `the SimpLEX draft` `theoretical examination` EQUALS JUST 273
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the SimpLEX draft` `practical examination`   EQUALS JUST 194

-- #5
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `theoretical examination` 273
-- #6
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `practical examination` 194
-- #7, both halves of "theoretical or practical"
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 40
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40
-- #8, and the worked example
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `theoretical examination` 0
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `practical examination` 0
-- underpayment is not payment "in full" (reg. 4)
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the SimpLEX draft` `theoretical examination` 272

§ `Tier 2 -- the same scenarios against the Regulations as made`

-- The theoretical examination had NO fee in the Regulations as made, so
-- reg. 4 has nothing to withhold: scenario #8's candidate, who did not pay,
-- is admitted to the theoretical examination.
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as made` `theoretical examination` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as made` `theoretical examination` 0
-- The practical examination and its fee survived unchanged.
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as made` `practical examination` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as made` `practical examination` 194
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as made` `practical examination` 0
-- The appeal fee attaches to "the examination score", and the only examination
-- the text as made knows is the practical one (reg. 1, and (b)'s own pointer to (a)).
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a practical examination score`   EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a practical examination score` 40
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a practical examination score` 0
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as made` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 0
-- Licence and foreign-expert fees are as drafted.
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as made` `issue or renewal of a licence`          EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as made` `temporary licence for a foreign expert` EQUALS JUST 398

§ `Tier 2 -- the same scenarios against the Regulations as amended`

-- The 5786 amendment put the theoretical examination fee back, at 158 rather
-- than the draft's 273, so scenario #8 refuses again -- and #5's candidate,
-- who paid the draft's 273, has overpaid.
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination` EQUALS JUST 158
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination` 0
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination` 158
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination` 273
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination` 157
-- The appeal fee MOVED: as amended it attaches to the theoretical score and no
-- longer to the practical one.
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `appeal against a practical examination score`   EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT     `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as amended` `appeal against a practical examination score` 0
#ASSERT NOT `the service may be provided` `the Regulations as amended` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` 0
-- Nothing else moved between as-made and as-amended.
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `practical examination`                        EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `issue or renewal of a licence`                 EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `temporary licence for a foreign expert`        EQUALS JUST 398

§ `Tier 2 -- what the three texts say, side by side`

#EVAL `the fee under` `the SimpLEX draft`          `theoretical examination`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as made`    `theoretical examination`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `theoretical examination`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the SimpLEX draft`          `appeal against a practical examination score`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as made`    `appeal against a practical examination score`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `appeal against a practical examination score`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as made`    `appeal against a theoretical examination score`
#EVAL `the fee under` `the Regulations as amended` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`
